*PPD-Adobe: "4.3"
*%
*% Brother PT-P700 CUPS PPD (unofficial, community-written)
*%
*% Not affiliated with or endorsed by Brother Industries, Ltd. "Brother"
*% and "P-touch" are trademarks of Brother Industries, Ltd. This PPD
*% drives the printer via the rastertoptp700 filter included in this
*% project; see README.md for install instructions and known
*% limitations. USB only -- the PT-P700 has no Bluetooth/WiFi.
*%
*% UNCONFIRMED ON REAL HARDWARE beyond what tools/test_print.py has
*% validated directly against a PT-P700 unit -- see README.md's "Other
*% Brother P-touch models" section before relying on this for
*% production prints. The PT-P710BT-specific fixes this project's
*% history documents (compression command, cut bit, colorspace,
*% orientation) are CUPS/macOS pipeline findings expected to apply
*% here too; the pin-alignment trim and feed margin (in
*% filter/rastertoptp700) are mechanical properties of one specific
*% unit and are NOT yet confirmed for the PT-P700.
*%
*FormatVersion: "4.3"
*FileVersion: "1.0"
*LanguageVersion: English
*LanguageEncoding: ISO8859-1
*PCFileName: "BRPTP700.PPD"
*Manufacturer: "Brother"
*Product: "(PT-P700)"
*cupsVersion: 2.0
*cupsSNMPSupplies: False
*cupsLanguages: "en"
*ModelName: "Brother PT-P700"
*ShortNickName: "Brother PT-P700"
*NickName: "Brother PT-P700, Raster (unofficial)"
*PSVersion: "(3010.000) 0"
*LanguageLevel: "3"
*ColorDevice: False
*DefaultColorSpace: Gray
*FileSystem: False
*Throughput: "1"
*TTRasterizer: Type42
*cupsManualCopies: True
*cupsFilter2: "application/vnd.cups-raster application/vnd.brother-ptp700-raster 0 rastertoptp700"

*% PageSize/PageRegion/ImageableArea/PaperDimension are declared WIDE
*% (length axis first, tape-width axis second) rather than narrow-tall
*% (tape-width first). Real hardware test: with tape-width-first (the
*% original layout here), cgpdftoraster's own auto-rotation heuristic for
*% narrow/tall pages kicked in and rendered text sized for *vertical*
*% reading (using the long axis as line-length) -- simply rotating that
*% output back would need rescaling, not just a rotate/mirror, since the
*% text was already sized assuming ~40mm of line length. Declaring the
*% page wide up front avoids triggering that heuristic, so cgpdftoraster
*% renders normal horizontal text sized for the tape-width axis as line
*% height. The filter (rastertoptp700) reads tape width from cupsHEIGHT
*% accordingly (see nearest_media() call there), and transposes the
*% raster grid to match the printer's line-per-tape-width-scan format.
*% Six generic length steps per tape width (20/40/60/80/100/150mm), plus
*% a few user-requested fixed sizes matching specific real label lengths
*% (12mm: 25/43/55/110mm; 18mm: 43mm; 24mm: 110mm) -- since macOS/CUPS's
*% Paper Size is always ONE combined (width x length) choice, there's no
*% way to offer independent width and length pickers, on this or any
*% other printer. Continuous tape has no fixed length, so the generic
*% steps are generous upper bounds, not fixed output sizes: the filter's
*% "Automatic Length" feature (see *AutoLength below) trims whatever
*% blank tape a job's actual content doesn't use, so picking a step at
*% least as big as your content just works, without needing "Manage
*% Custom Sizes" for the common case. Only content LONGER than 150mm (or
*% needing a length between these steps for its own sake) needs a Custom
*% size instead (see README.md's "Custom label length" section) --
*% Custom sizes accept any length, not just 20mm steps.
*OpenUI *PageSize/Tape Width: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 10 AnySetup *PageSize
*DefaultPageSize: mm12
*PageSize mm3.5-20/3.5mm Tape (20mm): "<</PageSize[57 10]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*PageSize mm3.5-40/3.5mm Tape (40mm): "<</PageSize[113 10]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*PageSize mm3.5-60/3.5mm Tape (60mm): "<</PageSize[170 10]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*PageSize mm3.5-80/3.5mm Tape (80mm): "<</PageSize[227 10]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*PageSize mm3.5/3.5mm Tape (100mm): "<</PageSize[283 10]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*PageSize mm3.5-long/3.5mm Tape (150mm (long)): "<</PageSize[425 10]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*PageSize mm6-20/6mm Tape (20mm): "<</PageSize[57 17]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*PageSize mm6-40/6mm Tape (40mm): "<</PageSize[113 17]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*PageSize mm6-60/6mm Tape (60mm): "<</PageSize[170 17]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*PageSize mm6-80/6mm Tape (80mm): "<</PageSize[227 17]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*PageSize mm6/6mm Tape (100mm): "<</PageSize[283 17]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*PageSize mm6-long/6mm Tape (150mm (long)): "<</PageSize[425 17]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*PageSize mm9-20/9mm Tape (20mm): "<</PageSize[57 26]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*PageSize mm9-40/9mm Tape (40mm): "<</PageSize[113 26]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*PageSize mm9-60/9mm Tape (60mm): "<</PageSize[170 26]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*PageSize mm9-80/9mm Tape (80mm): "<</PageSize[227 26]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*PageSize mm9/9mm Tape (100mm): "<</PageSize[283 26]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*PageSize mm9-long/9mm Tape (150mm (long)): "<</PageSize[425 26]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*PageSize mm12-20/12mm Tape (20mm): "<</PageSize[57 34]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*PageSize mm12-25/12mm Tape (25mm): "<</PageSize[71 34]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
